#: src/shell/HelpPage.tsx
msgid "The same menu offers <0>Export as Markdown</0> and <1>Export as JSON</1>. Both are built in your browser from the conversation already on screen, so nothing is sent anywhere and it works offline. Markdown is the branch you are reading, one section per turn, with attachments and tool calls named rather than embedded. JSON carries the same messages as the API sent them, plus every other branch of the conversation. The file is named after the conversation’s title. Everything on your account at once is under <2>Settings › Data</2>."
msgstr "The same menu offers <0>Export as Markdown</0> and <1>Export as JSON</1>. Both are built in your browser from the conversation already on screen, so nothing is sent anywhere and it works offline. Markdown is the branch you are reading, one section per turn, with attachments and tool calls named rather than embedded. JSON carries the same messages as the API sent them, plus every other branch of the conversation. The file is named after the conversation’s title. Everything on your account at once is under <2>Settings › Data</2>."

#: src/shell/HelpPage.tsx
msgid "The same models are reachable from your own code: the API speaks the OpenAI chat-completions format, so any OpenAI client works with a MatterWave key from <0>Settings › API keys</0>. The <1>developer portal</1> has the quickstart, the reference and the SDKs."
msgstr "The same models are reachable from your own code: the API speaks the OpenAI chat-completions format, so any OpenAI client works with a MatterWave key from <0>Settings › API keys</0>. The <1>developer portal</1> has the quickstart, the reference and the SDKs."

